---
// biome-ignore-all lint/suspicious/noUnknownAttribute: Astro templates use native HTML attributes.
type Props = Record<string, never>;
---

<section aria-labelledby="services-title" class="dark-section" id="expertise">
  <div class="services page-shell">
    <div class="service-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">03 / What we do</p>
      <h2 id="services-title">
        The right words.<br>The right form.<br>The whole picture.
      </h2>
      <p>
        From the first strategic question to the last line of code. One
        connected team, no lost-in-translation handovers.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="#contact"
        >Discuss your brief
        <span aria-hidden="true" class="arrow-icon">↗</span></a
      >
    </div>
    <div class="service-list">
      <article class="service-item">
        <span class="service-number">01</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Find your position.</h3>
          <p>
            Get specific about what you do, who it matters to, and why they
            should choose you. A useful foundation, not a 100-page deck.
          </p>
          <small>Research / Positioning / Brand architecture / Messaging</small>
        </div>
        <span aria-hidden="true" class="service-arrow arrow-icon">↗</span>
      </article>
      <article class="service-item">
        <span class="service-number">02</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Give it expression.</h3>
          <p>
            Build an identity that makes your difference tangible. Distinctive
            enough to be noticed. Practical enough to be used every day.
          </p>
          <small
            >Naming / Visual identity / Verbal identity / Brand systems</small
          >
        </div>
        <span aria-hidden="true" class="service-arrow arrow-icon">↗</span>
      </article>
      <article class="service-item">
        <span class="service-number">03</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Put it to work.</h3>
          <p>
            Turn your brand into a clear digital experience, built around real
            buyer questions and the people who’ll keep it running.
          </p>
          <small
            >UX & content / Web design / Development / Launch support</small
          >
        </div>
        <span aria-hidden="true" class="service-arrow arrow-icon">↗</span>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
